<article class="finding" id="f4">
<div class="fhead">
<span class="fid">F4</span>
<span class="label fail rule"><span class="shape"></span>Rule broken</span>
<span class="foracle">same_as_base</span>
<span class="fcount">5 cases · c-0014, c-0017, c-0046, c-0061, c-0074 · already minimal</span>
</div>
<h3>The importer reported a different latest_glucose when the entries were in a different order.</h3>
<div class="fbody">
<div class="fleft">
<div class="facts">
<span class="k">Expected</span><span class="v">latest_glucose = 7.2 from Observation&#x2f;obs-glucose-3</span>
<span class="k">Got</span><span class="v">latest_glucose = 6.8 from Observation&#x2f;obs-glucose-2</span>
<span class="k">Mutation</span><span class="v"><code>bundle.reorder_entries</code></span>
<span class="k">Change</span><span class="v">entries shuffled, 9 of 12 in a new position</span>
<span class="k">Shrunk</span><span class="v">8 entries not needed to fail were removed</span>
<span class="k">Check</span><span class="v">Built in. Reads &#x2f;latest&#x2f;synthetic-glucose from your target&#x27;s view</span>

</div>
<table class="layers">
<caption>Validation of the shrunk bundle</caption>
<tbody>
<tr><td>R4 JSON schema 4.0.1</td><td class="r">Valid</td></tr>
<tr><td>References inside the bundle</td><td class="r">All resolve</td></tr>
<tr><td>HL7 validator</td><td class="r caution">Not run, add --strict</td></tr>

</tbody>
</table>
<p class="why">Likely cause: the importer treats bundle order as time order. FHIR gives entry order no meaning in a collection bundle.</p>
</div>
<div class="fright">

